      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a net prior year strengthening of GBP 20.059 million in 2020, representing 1.19% of its opening gross claims outstanding. This adverse run-off deviation was observed across both direct insurance and inwards reinsurance business lines, with a mix of releases and strengthenings at the line of business level. The report notes \"adverse development on business written outside of the current underwriting year\" and \"single large losses\" as contributing factors to adverse prior year development. The year was significantly impacted by the COVID-19 pandemic, resulting in GBP 84.9 million net claims, and a record-breaking hurricane season including Hurricane Laura (GBP 27.2 million), Hurricanes Zeta and Sally, and other US weather events. The largest gross premiums written were in Fire & other damage to property, Third party liability, and Reinsurance inwards.",
